>> title: Borscht, Instant Pot
>> category: Soups
>> tags: beets, beef, cabbage, ukrainian, winter, instant pot, pressure cooker
>> counters: Instant Pot
>> aka: instant pot borscht, pressure cooker borscht, instant pot beet soup, borsch, borshch, barszcz, beet soup, red borscht, Ukrainian borscht
>> servings: 6
>> dish: borscht
>> kit: Instant Pot
>> time: 2 hr
>> slack: forgiving — the beets are the one thing that can be overcooked here, so they finish with the lid off where you can taste them
>> washing-up: the Instant Pot, a plate for the browned short ribs

>> step: brown the short ribs on Sauté 10 min
Brown @beef short ribs{2%lb}(900 g; bone-in) in the #Instant Pot{} on the highest Sauté setting in their own fat ~brown{10%min}, in two batches, and lift them out.

>> step: fry the onion and carrot in the fat 8 min
Fry @yellow onion{1%large}(chopped) and @carrot{1%large}(grated) in @unsalted butter{2%Tbs} in the same pot ~fry{8%min}, scraping the brown from the bottom as they go.

>> step: return the ribs to the stock — 40 min at high pressure
Return @&(~2)short ribs{} to @&(~1)vegetables{} with @beef stock{6%cups}(1.4 L), lock the lid and ~pressure cook{40%min} at high pressure.

>> step: wait out the natural release 15 min, pull the meat off the bones
Let @&(~1)pot{} ~natural release{15%min}, then pull the meat off the bones and discard them.

>> step: simmer the beets, potato and cabbage, lid off, 20 min
Simmer @&(~1)pot{} with the lid off on Sauté ~simmer{20%min} with @beets{1 1/2%lb}(700 g; peeled and grated), @tomato paste{2%Tbs}, @cider vinegar{2%Tbs}, @russet potatoes{3/4%lb}(340 g; cubed) and @green cabbage{3%cups}(shredded).

>> step: season, sour cream at the table
Season @&(~1)borscht{} with @garlic{2%cloves}(minced), @kosher salt{2%tsp} and @fresh dill{3%Tbs}(chopped), and pass @sour cream{2/3%cup}(160 g) at the table.
